    "narrative": "For the June 6th slate, the Austin Waves lineup centers on capitalizing against the favorable matchup provided by Jack Kochanowicz, vaulting **Kyle Tucker** (78.74) and **Andy Pages** (70.49) to the top of our daily hierarchy. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most potent asset, benefiting from a soft SP_xERA of 5.12, while **Andy Pages** derives significant value from his assumed #2 spot in the order, providing high-leverage opportunities despite facing a pitcher who excels at holding runners. **Gunnar Henderson** (64.40) also commands attention; while he faces a tougher arm in Fisher, the 85% stolen base success rate against the opposing battery makes him a critical engine for our scarcity-driven strategy, particularly with his dynamic platoon advantage providing a +14% boost.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved the exclusion of **Brayan Rocchio** (43.54). While he offered a higher floor than **Dominic Smith** (42.18), his projected placement in the #9 hole dragged his score below the desired threshold, whereas **Dominic Smith** maintains a situational utility in the #5 spot that the optimizer prioritized for potential RBI volume. We must remain vigilant regarding **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Josh Jung**; because their lineups are technically \"Pending,\" any late-order demotions could rapidly erode their efficiency scores. We are effectively betting on the projected lineup spots to sustain these values, particularly for **Miguel Vargas**, who benefits from wind blowing out at the park to bolster his 61.55 rating despite a challenging catcher matchup.",
